@startuml component-overview
' DASS — logical architecture.
' Carries the constraints that a box diagram alone would lose: which component may
' reach which database endpoint, and why each queue exists separately.

title DASS — logical architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #BBBBBB
}

actor "Browser /\nAPI client" as Client

package "Edge" {
  [Traefik\n:8443 TLS] as Traefik
}

package "Application" {
  [Next.js frontend\n:3000] as Frontend
  [FastAPI API server\n:8000] as API
  [Scheduler\nsingle leader] as Scheduler
  [Autoscaler\nmode 1 only] as Autoscaler
}

package "Queues (SQS / LocalStack)" {
  queue "normal\non-demand runs" as QNormal
  queue "scheduled\ncron dispatches" as QSched
  queue "retry\nre-runs" as QRetry
}

package "Workers" {
  [Worker pool\nper queue] as Worker
  [Job container\nalpine / curl] as JobContainer
}

package "Storage" {
  [PgBouncer\n:6432 transaction pooling] as PgBouncer
  database "PostgreSQL primary\nsource of truth" as Primary
  database "PostgreSQL replica\nread-only" as Replica
}

Client -down-> Traefik
Traefik -down-> Frontend
Traefik -down-> API : /api /health\n/metrics /docs
Frontend -right-> API : server-side\nrewrites

API -down-> QNormal : trigger,\ncreate one-time job
Scheduler -down-> QSched : cron dispatch
Scheduler -down-> QNormal : dependency (DAG) dispatch
Autoscaler -right-> Worker : add / remove

QNormal -down-> Worker
QSched -down-> Worker
QRetry -down-> Worker
Worker -up-> QRetry : re-enqueue\non failure
Worker -right-> JobContainer : run runtime_spec

API -down-> PgBouncer : writes +\nread-after-write
Worker -down-> PgBouncer : claim, heartbeat, result
PgBouncer -down-> Primary
Scheduler -down-> Primary : **direct**, bypasses PgBouncer
API -down-> Replica : plain SELECTs
Primary -right[#999999]-> Replica : streaming\nreplication

note right of Scheduler
  **Why the scheduler bypasses PgBouncer**
  Leader election holds a //session-level//
  advisory lock. Transaction pooling hands the
  server connection back at commit, which drops
  the lock and elects several leaders at once.
end note

note right of Worker
  **Claim protocol**
  1. ""UPDATE ... WHERE status='pending'"" —
     atomic, exactly one worker wins
  2. A heartbeat extends the DB lock //and// the
     queue message visibility together, so a
     crashed worker loses both at once and the
     task is reclaimable within one window
  3. On failure, re-enqueue to the retry queue
     until ""max_retries"" is reached
end note

note bottom of Replica
  Reads fall back to the primary when the session
  has just written. With no replica configured,
  one engine is shared instead of a second pool
  being opened against the same server.
end note
@enduml
